$0(){return A.jR(this.a,"# Cipher \u2014 three oscillators encrypted by two clocks and three rings.\nname Cipher\n#\n# Three voices feed a stack of three SyncRing modulators. Two\n# Sequencer8s act as cipher keys: seqFast keys ring1, seqSlow keys\n# ring2, and ring3 runs continuously (gate left unconnected \u2192 open by\n# default \u2192 modulation every sample). Three normalize laws colour the\n# three layers \u2014 peak / signed / rms \u2014 so each modulation stage has\n# its own gain character.\n#\n# Two Copy2Pcm fan-outs share voice1 and voice2 between the gated cascade\n# (ring1 \u2192 ring2) and the always-on layer (ring3). Mix2Pcm weds the two\n# layers; BandPass narrows the wash; Delay smears it into the rests.\n#\n# Coprime BPMs (175 and 71) mean the overall pattern drifts \u2014 the\n# cipher never repeats the same key combination twice.\n\n# --- Two clocks (the cipher keys) ---\nfilter Sequencer8 seqFast\nknob seqFast bpm 175.0\nknob seqFast step_1 true\nknob seqFast step_2 false\nknob seqFast step_3 true\nknob seqFast step_4 true\nknob seqFast step_5 false\nknob seqFast step_6 true\nknob seqFast step_7 true\nknob seqFast step_8 false\n\nfilter Sequencer8 seqSlow\nknob seqSlow bpm 71.0\nknob seqSlow step_1 true\nknob seqSlow step_2 false\nknob seqSlow step_3 false\nknob seqSlow step_4 true\nknob seqSlow step_5 true\nknob seqSlow step_6 false\nknob seqSlow step_7 true\nknob seqSlow step_8 true\n\n# --- Three voices ---\nfilter Timer555 voice1\nknob voice1 freq 196.0\nknob voice1 duty_cycle 0.32\n\nfilter ClassicOscillator voice2\nknob voice2 freq 277.0\nknob voice2 waveform 2          # Sawtooth\n\nfilter Timer555 voice3\nknob voice3 freq 58.0\nknob voice3 duty_cycle 0.5\n\n# --- Fan voice1 and voice2 between the gated cascade and the always-on\n# layer, so the same source material appears in both with different\n# modulation faces.\nfilter Copy2Pcm v1cp\npatch voice1 out_pcm -> v1cp in_pcm\n\nfilter Copy2Pcm v2cp\npatch voice2 out_pcm -> v2cp in_pcm\n\n# --- Ring 1: voice1 \xd7 voice2, gated by seqFast. Peak normalize keeps\n# the chatter bounded so the cascade downstream doesn't snowball.\nfilter SyncRing ring1\nknob ring1 depth 0.85\nknob ring1 normalize 1          # Peak\npatch v1cp out_pcm_a -> ring1 in_pcm_a_carrier\npatch v2cp out_pcm_a -> ring1 in_pcm_b_modulator\npatch seqFast out_gate -> ring1 in_gate\n\n# --- Ring 2: ring1 (chatter) \xd7 voice3 (sub-bass), gated by seqSlow.\n# Signed normalize locks polarity to the chatter while the sub pushes\n# magnitude \u2014 gives a polarity-coupled rasp, the bass impression\n# without classic AM symmetry.\nfilter SyncRing ring2\nknob ring2 depth 0.9\nknob ring2 normalize 3          # Signed\npatch ring1 out_pcm -> ring2 in_pcm_a_carrier\npatch voice3 out_pcm -> ring2 in_pcm_b_modulator\npatch seqSlow out_gate -> ring2 in_gate\n\n# --- Ring 3: voice1 \xd7 voice2 again, but ungated (gate socket left\n# disconnected \u2014 defaults to open). RMS normalize preserves average\n# energy so the always-on layer breathes evenly under the gated chain.\nfilter SyncRing ring3\nknob ring3 depth 0.55\nknob ring3 normalize 2          # RMS\npatch v1cp out_pcm_b -> ring3 in_pcm_a_carrier\npatch v2cp out_pcm_b -> ring3 in_pcm_b_modulator\n\n# --- Wed the gated cascade with the always-on layer.\nfilter Mix2Pcm wed\nknob wed normalize true\npatch ring2 out_pcm -> wed in_pcm_a\npatch ring3 out_pcm -> wed in_pcm_b\n\n# --- Tame the wash and smear it into the rests.\nfilter BandPass tame\nknob tame low_cutoff 220.0\nknob tame high_cutoff 2600.0\npatch wed out_pcm -> tame in_pcm\n\nfilter Delay smear\nknob smear time 0.33\nknob smear feedback 0.55\nknob smear mix 0.5\npatch tame out_pcm -> smear in_pcm\n\nfilter Volume master\nknob master volume 0.55\npatch smear out_pcm -> master in_pcm\n\noutput master out_pcm\n\n"+A.hZ())},
